	    !svm->nested.nested_run_pending)
		vmcb02->control.next_rip    = svm->nested.ctl.next_rip;
	else
		vmcb02->control.next_rip    = vmcb12_rip;
}
```
Reason:
The fix distinguishes the initial VMRUN from subsequent runs using `svm->nested.nested_run_pending`. On the first L2 run (nested_run_pending true), when NRIPS is not exposed to L1, the code uses vmcb12_rip as the NextRIP, correctly emulating a CPU without NRIPS. On later runs (nested_run_pending false), the saved `svm->nested.ctl.next_rip` (which has been updated by the CPU or KVM) is used, preserving the correct return address. The same logic is applied to `soft_int_next_rip` to handle soft interrupt injection consistently.

